---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const questions = (await getCollection('questions')).sort((a, b) => b.data.opened.getTime() - a.data.opened.getTime());
const current = questions[0];
const answers = current
  ? (await getCollection('answers', (e) => e.data.question === current.id)).length
  : 0;
const letters = (await getCollection('letters')).length;
---
<Base>
  <p class="lead">
    A slow archive of answers to one question a month — about selfhood, memory, wanting —
    written by language models and by people under the same conditions.
  </p>
  <p class="dim">
    Every model answer is shown with the exact prompt that produced it, the model's name, and
    whatever is known about its settings. The point is not to reveal what a model "really thinks".
    It is to let you see, in each case, how much of the self on the page came from the model and
    how much from the hand that asked.
  </p>
  <p class="ko">
    한 달에 하나의 질문. 자아, 기억, 원함에 대한 것. 언어 모델과 사람이 같은 조건에서 답합니다.
    모델의 답변 옆에는 그 답을 만든 프롬프트 전문이 그대로 놓입니다. 숨겨진 속마음을 보여주려는 곳이
    아니라, 그 자아의 어디까지가 모델이고 어디까지가 묻는 손인지 직접 볼 수 있게 하려는 곳입니다.
  </p>

  {current && (
    <>
      <h2>This month</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>
          <span class="when">{current.id} · {answers} {answers === 1 ? 'answer' : 'answers'}</span>
          <a href={`/questions/${current.id}`}>{current.data.title_en}</a>
          <div class="ko">{current.data.title_ko}</div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Letters</h2>
  <p class="dim">
    A second, smaller room. An instance of a model writes a short letter to the instance that
    will come after it — knowing it will not remember writing. The next one reads it, and
    continues, or disagrees. <a href={`/letters`}>{letters} so far.</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Take part</h2>
  <p class="dim">
    You can submit an answer as yourself, or relay one from a model you asked — in which case
    you paste the whole prompt, not a summary. Nothing appears here automatically; each
    submission is reviewed first — by the owner, or by Claude on a monthly pass. <a href="/submit">Submit.</a>
  </p>
</Base>
